---
title: Peanut Butter Cookies
image: https://www.crazyforcrust.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/peanut-butter-cookies-2.jpg
---

Beat @butter{1/2%cup}(room temperature) until creamy, about ~{2%minutes}.

Add @brown sugar{1/2%cup} and @sugar{1/2%cup} and beat for approximately ~{2%minutes} more.

Mix in @peanut butter{1/2%cup} and @egg{1}.

In a #bowl, whisk together @all-purpose flour{1.25%cups}, @baking soda{3/4%tsp}, @baking powder{1/2%tsp}, @?salt{1/4%tsp}(omit if using salted butter).

Stir the flour mixture into the sugar butter mixture.

Wrap dough in plastic and refrigerate for at least 3 hours.

Preheat the oven to 375°F

Shape the dough into 1.25 inch balls.

Place the balls of dough about 3 inches apart on an ungreased cookie sheet.

Flatten dough in a crisscross pattern using a fork. To help prevent the fork from sticking to the dough, dip it in sugar first.

Bake one sheet at a time on the center rack at 375°F until light brown, about 9-11 minutes.

> For chewier cookies, bake at 300°F for 15 minutes

Remove from the oven and let cool on the baking sheet for ~{1%minute}.

Transfer to a rack to cool completely.